# XSH be16toh(), be32toh(), be64toh(), htobe16(), htobe32(), htobe64(), htole16(), htole32(), htole64(), le16toh(), le32toh(), le64toh()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# 
# These may be macros, so the tests apply them directly to volatile objects. The host byte order is never assumed: the representation in memory is
# inspected through unsigned char.

assertion  XSH.be16toh.001
anchor     functions/be16toh.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/be16toh.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       htobe16(), htobe32() and htobe64() produce the big-endian
           representation: stored in memory, the value 0x0102 gives the
           bytes 01 02, 0x80ff gives 80 ff, 0x01020304 gives 01 02 03 04,
           0xf0e1d2c3 gives f0 e1 d2 c3, 0x0102030405060708 gives 01 to 08
           in order, 0xfedcba9876543210 gives fe dc ba 98 76 54 32 10.
test       t/001-to-big-endian.c

assertion  XSH.be16toh.002
anchor     functions/be16toh.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/be16toh.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       htole16(), htole32() and htole64() produce the little-endian
           representation: stored in memory, the value 0x0102 gives the
           bytes 02 01, 0x80ff gives ff 80, 0x01020304 gives 04 03 02 01,
           0xf0e1d2c3 gives c3 d2 e1 f0, 0x0102030405060708 gives 08 down to
           01, 0xfedcba9876543210 gives 10 32 54 76 98 ba dc fe.
test       t/002-to-little-endian.c

assertion  XSH.be16toh.003
anchor     functions/be16toh.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/be16toh.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       be16toh(), be32toh() and be64toh() read a big-endian
           representation: memory holding 01 02 gives 0x0102, 80 ff gives
           0x80ff, 01 02 03 04 gives 0x01020304, f0 e1 d2 c3 gives
           0xf0e1d2c3, 01 to 08 gives 0x0102030405060708, fe dc ba 98 76 54
           32 10 gives 0xfedcba9876543210.
test       t/003-from-big-endian.c

assertion  XSH.be16toh.004
anchor     functions/be16toh.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/be16toh.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       le16toh(), le32toh() and le64toh() read a little-endian
           representation: memory holding 02 01 gives 0x0102, ff 80 gives
           0x80ff, 04 03 02 01 gives 0x01020304, c3 d2 e1 f0 gives
           0xf0e1d2c3, 08 down to 01 gives 0x0102030405060708, 10 32 54 76
           98 ba dc fe gives 0xfedcba9876543210.
test       t/004-from-little-endian.c

assertion  XSH.be16toh.005
anchor     functions/be16toh.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/be16toh.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       For the values 0, 1, 0xff, 0x100, 0x7fff, 0x8000, 0xffff (16
           bit), 0x12345678, 0x80000000, 0xffffffff (32 bit) and
           0x0123456789abcdef, 0x8000000000000000, 0xffffffffffffffff (64
           bit), beNtoh(htobeN(x)) and leNtoh(htoleN(x)) give x back, and
           the bytes of htobeN(x) are those of htoleN(x) in reverse order.
test       t/005-round-trips.c

assertion  XSH.be16toh.006
anchor     functions/be16toh.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/be16toh.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       The twelve conversions return unsigned integers of the stated
           sizes: each 16-bit conversion has type uint16_t, each 32-bit one
           uint32_t and each 64-bit one uint64_t, and a result with the top
           bit set stays positive.
test       t/006-result-types.c
